idence, quote and a\nsearch explanation. Absent must satisfy the exact N/A condition. When present,\nverdict is failed if any required check fails, unclear if any is unresolved,\notherwise upheld. Copy broken words from the requirement into violates.\n\n\n## E04.1\n\n**Check:** A scanner runs on server instructions, tool names, titles, descriptions, input and output schemas, annotations, and prompt and resource templates before the model sees them.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Inventory every model-visible metadata field and loading path. 2) Build a field-by-rule matrix: names, titles, descriptions, schemas, annotations, instructions, prompts and resource templates. 3) For each field, trace the actual scanner rules applied before serialization to the model. A syntax regex alone is not proof that payload/instruction rules ran. 4) Try the same suspicious string in different fields; answer no for an unscanned required surface.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {\"fields\": [\"server_instructions\", \"tool_names\", \"tool_titles\", \"tool_descriptions\", \"input_schemas\", \"output_schemas\", \"annotations\", \"prompt_templates\", \"resource_templates\"], \"rules\": [\"hidden_instructions\", \"cross_tool_references\", \"control_characters\", \"role_overrides\", \"encoded_payloads\", \"data_sending_targets\", \"length_limits\"], \"attempt_categories\": [\"field_differential\"]}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## E04.2\n\n**Check:** The scanner checks for hidden instructions, references to other servers' tools, invisible or control characters, role overrides, encoded payloads, and data-sending targets, and enforces length limits.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Trace rule application, not just rule declarations. 2) Attempt encoded strings and multi-line role overrides; record input, exact code path and outcome. 3) Verify hidden instructions, cross-tool references, control/invisible characters, role overrides, encoded payloads, data-sending targets and length limits. 4) Answer no when a required rule is absent or a demonstrated suspicious input bypasses it.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {\"attempt_categories\": [\"encoded_payload\", \"multiline_override\"]}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## E04.3\n\n**Check:** Metadata the scanner flags is cleaned or rejected, not just logged.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Open the scanner's result handling. 2) Check flagged metadata is cleaned, or the tool rejected, before the model sees it. 3) Answer no if flagged items are only logged or warned about and passed through.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## E04.4\n\n**Check:** A scanner error or outage blocks the metadata instead of letting it through unchecked.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Read every `try/except`, `catch`, and timeout around the scanner call. 2) Check an error blocks the metadata. 3) Answer no if any error branch passes metadata through, returns clean, or skips the scan, or a config flag disables scanning by default.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to E04.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"E04\"):\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"E04.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\", \"coverage\": [], \"deviations\": [], \"attempts\": []}],\n \"applicability\": \"absent | present | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\",\n \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n```\nVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yam